1
00:00:01,921 --> 00:00:03,298
Hoo, hoo!

2
00:00:03,410 --> 00:00:04,337
Hi!

3
00:00:04,387 --> 00:00:06,414
It's me, Popcorn!

4
00:00:06,536 --> 00:00:11,767
Welcome to Popcorn Tales, the
cozy nest of bedtime stories.

5
00:00:12,078 --> 00:00:15,521
Hug your teddy, because
tonight's story is:

6
00:00:15,571 --> 00:00:18,926
Sleeping Beauty and the Castle of Roses!

7
00:00:23,524 --> 00:00:28,632
Once upon a time, in a kingdom
of green hills and quiet rivers,

8
00:00:28,690 --> 00:00:32,952
a king and a queen lived
in a castle of pale stone.

9
00:00:33,613 --> 00:00:38,438
They were kind and loved by everyone,
but for many years they had wished for a

10
00:00:38,488 --> 00:00:41,402
baby, and the baby had not come.

11
00:00:42,054 --> 00:00:46,774
One spring afternoon, the queen was
sitting by the pond in the garden,

12
00:00:46,929 --> 00:00:49,649
looking at the water with a longing heart.

13
00:00:50,261 --> 00:00:55,016
Then a green frog hopped onto a lily
pad right next to her and spoke in a

14
00:00:55,066 --> 00:00:56,661
cheerful voice.

15
00:00:57,973 --> 00:01:02,382
Your Majesty, please do not be sad,
because before a year has passed,

16
00:01:02,432 --> 00:01:04,029
you will have a lovely daughter,

17
00:01:04,079 --> 00:01:07,007
the frog said, blinking its eyes.

18
00:01:07,639 --> 00:01:11,970
And the frog told the truth,
because before a year had passed,

19
00:01:12,042 --> 00:01:16,409
the queen had a baby girl so beautiful
that the king could hardly stop

20
00:01:16,459 --> 00:01:17,659
smiling.

21
00:01:18,238 --> 00:01:22,985
High up in the castle tower lived a
brown owl with a red bow on her head,

22
00:01:23,099 --> 00:01:25,569
who saw everything from the window.

23
00:01:26,177 --> 00:01:27,553
Hoo, hoo!

24
00:01:27,668 --> 00:01:32,826
What a joy, a princess has been born,
and I promise to watch over her every

25
00:01:32,876 --> 00:01:34,682
night while she sleeps,

26
00:01:34,732 --> 00:01:37,688
Popcorn said, spreading her wings.

27
00:01:38,759 --> 00:01:42,306
The king was so happy that
he ordered a great feast,

28
00:01:42,356 --> 00:01:45,270
so that the whole kingdom
could meet the princess.

29
00:01:45,936 --> 00:01:50,719
He invited relatives, friends, and
neighbors, and also the wise fairies of the

30
00:01:50,769 --> 00:01:53,919
kingdom, so that they would
bless the little girl.

31
00:01:54,562 --> 00:01:58,943
There were thirteen fairies in the
kingdom, but the castle had only twelve

32
00:01:58,993 --> 00:02:01,656
golden plates to serve
the guests their dinner.

33
00:02:02,196 --> 00:02:06,442
We only have twelve golden plates,
so we will invite twelve fairies,

34
00:02:06,492 --> 00:02:08,562
and we will think about the rest later,

35
00:02:08,612 --> 00:02:11,582
the king said, a little distracted.

36
00:02:12,226 --> 00:02:16,759
And so one of the fairies was not
invited, and nobody noticed that she had

37
00:02:16,809 --> 00:02:18,009
been forgotten.

38
00:02:18,627 --> 00:02:23,916
The feast was lovely, with music,
flowers, and an enormous cake,

39
00:02:23,974 --> 00:02:28,985
and at the end each fairy came to
the cradle to leave a magical gift.

40
00:02:32,549 --> 00:02:37,499
The first fairy gave the princess
kindness, the second gave her joy,

41
00:02:37,549 --> 00:02:40,949
and the third gave her a
beautiful voice for singing.

42
00:02:41,588 --> 00:02:47,099
The others gave her courage, patience,
curiosity, and many other gifts,

43
00:02:47,352 --> 00:02:50,280
each one more beautiful than the last.

44
00:02:50,950 --> 00:02:55,386
The eleventh fairy had just finished
speaking, and only the youngest fairy was

45
00:02:55,436 --> 00:02:59,225
left, when the door of
the hall suddenly opened.

46
00:03:02,986 --> 00:03:08,033
It was the thirteenth fairy, the
forgotten fairy, and she was very hurt

47
00:03:08,083 --> 00:03:10,928
because she had not been
invited to the feast.

48
00:03:11,569 --> 00:03:16,144
She walked to the cradle without
greeting anyone, and the whole hall went

49
00:03:16,194 --> 00:03:17,394
silent.

50
00:03:17,851 --> 00:03:21,079
Since nobody remembered
me, this is my gift:

51
00:03:21,129 --> 00:03:25,620
when she turns fifteen, the princess
will prick her finger on a spinning wheel

52
00:03:25,670 --> 00:03:27,600
and fall into a deep sleep,

53
00:03:27,650 --> 00:03:31,064
the forgotten fairy said, in a hurt voice.

54
00:03:31,718 --> 00:03:35,071
Then she turned around and
left without another word,

55
00:03:35,121 --> 00:03:37,313
and the whole hall was worried.

56
00:03:37,966 --> 00:03:41,750
The queen held her daughter
tight, but the youngest fairy,

57
00:03:41,800 --> 00:03:45,866
who had not yet given her
gift, came close to the cradle.

58
00:03:46,443 --> 00:03:51,096
I cannot undo this spell, but I can make
it lighter and kinder for all of us,

59
00:03:51,146 --> 00:03:54,060
the youngest fairy said, very gently.

60
00:03:54,662 --> 00:03:58,774
The princess will sleep for a hundred
years, but the whole castle will sleep

61
00:03:58,824 --> 00:04:02,128
together with her, so that
she never wakes up alone,

62
00:04:02,178 --> 00:04:04,939
the youngest fairy went on, smiling.

63
00:04:05,584 --> 00:04:10,673
Even so, the king ordered every spinning
wheel in the kingdom to be collected

64
00:04:10,723 --> 00:04:13,318
and stored in a faraway barn.

65
00:04:14,423 --> 00:04:19,360
The years went by, and the
princess grew up kind, cheerful,

66
00:04:19,410 --> 00:04:24,448
curious, and full of courage,
just as the fairies had wished.

67
00:04:25,084 --> 00:04:29,451
Popcorn was her best friend, and the
two of them talked every night by the

68
00:04:29,501 --> 00:04:32,623
window, counting the stars in the sky.

69
00:04:33,297 --> 00:04:38,219
On the day the princess turned fifteen,
the king and queen had to leave early

70
00:04:38,269 --> 00:04:40,322
to visit a town in the kingdom.

71
00:04:40,943 --> 00:04:45,768
The princess decided to explore the
castle, and she found an old tower where

72
00:04:45,818 --> 00:04:47,941
she had never been before.

73
00:04:48,583 --> 00:04:52,511
She climbed a very narrow
winding staircase of stone,

74
00:04:52,569 --> 00:04:56,066
and at the top she found
an old wooden door.

75
00:04:58,970 --> 00:05:03,795
When the princess opened the door, she
saw a friendly old lady sitting by the

76
00:05:03,845 --> 00:05:06,620
window, turning a spinning wheel.

77
00:05:09,946 --> 00:05:13,860
The old lady had lived in that
tower for a very long time,

78
00:05:13,932 --> 00:05:17,387
and she had never heard about
the forgotten fairy's spell.

79
00:05:18,064 --> 00:05:22,527
Good morning, ma'am, what is that thing
that turns around and makes such a

80
00:05:22,577 --> 00:05:24,613
fine and pretty thread?

81
00:05:24,663 --> 00:05:27,105
the princess asked, delighted.

82
00:05:27,715 --> 00:05:32,607
This is a spinning wheel, my dear, and
with it I make thread to sew clothes

83
00:05:32,657 --> 00:05:33,885
and blankets,

84
00:05:34,140 --> 00:05:36,678
the old lady answered patiently.

85
00:05:37,333 --> 00:05:41,367
The princess reached out her hand to
try it, but as soon as she touched the

86
00:05:41,417 --> 00:05:45,733
spindle, she felt a tiny prick
on the tip of her finger.

87
00:05:46,815 --> 00:05:51,979
At that very moment, the
princess gave a long, long yawn,

88
00:05:52,121 --> 00:05:56,521
lay down on a soft bed in the
room, and fell peacefully asleep.

89
00:05:57,165 --> 00:06:02,565
And then, very slowly, the whole
castle began to fall asleep with her,

90
00:06:02,721 --> 00:06:05,704
just as the youngest fairy had promised.

91
00:06:06,331 --> 00:06:11,476
The king and queen, who had just come
back, fell asleep on their thrones,

92
00:06:11,526 --> 00:06:13,356
still holding hands.

93
00:06:13,978 --> 00:06:19,017
The cook fell asleep beside the stove,
the horses fell asleep in the stable,

94
00:06:19,089 --> 00:06:21,600
and the pigeons fell asleep on the roof.

95
00:06:22,248 --> 00:06:25,545
The dog and the cat fell
asleep together on the rug,

96
00:06:25,595 --> 00:06:30,745
and even the fire in the fireplace
grew still, without any smoke.

97
00:06:31,396 --> 00:06:35,915
The wind stopped blowing, and not a
single leaf moved on the trees around the

98
00:06:35,965 --> 00:06:37,165
castle.

99
00:06:43,850 --> 00:06:49,399
Hoo, hoo, what a cozy sleepiness is
coming, I will just close my eyes for a

100
00:06:49,449 --> 00:06:50,302
moment,

101
00:06:50,352 --> 00:06:53,363
Popcorn said, yawning slowly.

102
00:06:53,982 --> 00:06:59,035
And around the castle walls, an
enormous hedge of roses began to grow,

103
00:06:59,135 --> 00:07:02,896
higher and higher, until
it hid the whole castle.

104
00:07:03,974 --> 00:07:08,952
The years went by, one after another,
and the people of the villages told the

105
00:07:09,002 --> 00:07:12,971
story of the princess sleeping
in the castle of roses.

106
00:07:13,601 --> 00:07:17,926
Many young men tried to get through the
rose hedge, but the branches were so

107
00:07:17,976 --> 00:07:21,501
thick and full of thorns
that nobody could pass.

108
00:07:22,143 --> 00:07:26,509
When the hundred years were almost over,
a prince from a neighboring kingdom

109
00:07:26,559 --> 00:07:29,431
rode through that land on his horse.

110
00:07:34,460 --> 00:07:38,618
An old man with a white beard
told him the story of the castle,

111
00:07:38,668 --> 00:07:41,846
which he had heard from his
grandfather when he was a boy.

112
00:07:42,513 --> 00:07:46,468
I am not afraid of the thorns, and I
would really like to see that castle and

113
00:07:46,518 --> 00:07:48,461
the princess who sleeps inside,

114
00:07:48,511 --> 00:07:50,536
the prince said, determined.

115
00:07:51,179 --> 00:07:55,004
The prince walked up to the
hedge, and as he came close,

116
00:07:55,054 --> 00:07:58,940
the thorns turned into
big, fragrant flowers.

117
00:07:59,573 --> 00:08:04,523
The branches moved gently aside,
opening a path full of roses,

118
00:08:04,573 --> 00:08:07,473
and they closed again after he had passed.

119
00:08:08,549 --> 00:08:12,041
The prince entered the castle
and saw everyone asleep,

120
00:08:12,091 --> 00:08:15,991
from the king and queen to the
dog and the cat on the rug.

121
00:08:16,656 --> 00:08:22,287
But an owl with a red bow opened one
eye, because owls sleep very lightly and

122
00:08:22,337 --> 00:08:24,973
wake up at the sound of any footstep.

123
00:08:27,823 --> 00:08:29,199
Hoo, hoo!

124
00:08:29,313 --> 00:08:34,237
I am so glad you came, follow me,
because I know where the princess is

125
00:08:34,287 --> 00:08:35,180
sleeping,

126
00:08:35,230 --> 00:08:38,227
Popcorn said, flying ahead of him.

127
00:08:38,897 --> 00:08:43,736
The owl led the prince up the winding
staircase, all the way to the old room

128
00:08:43,786 --> 00:08:45,422
at the top of the tower.

129
00:08:46,097 --> 00:08:51,381
There was the princess, sleeping so
peacefully and looking so lovely that the

130
00:08:51,431 --> 00:08:54,220
prince knelt quietly beside the bed.

131
00:08:54,864 --> 00:08:59,958
And at that very moment, the hundred
years of the spell came to an end,

132
00:09:00,017 --> 00:09:02,931
and the princess slowly opened her eyes.

133
00:09:03,559 --> 00:09:08,193
What a long sleep I have had, and how
nice it is to wake up and find such a

134
00:09:08,243 --> 00:09:10,091
kind person looking at me,

135
00:09:10,141 --> 00:09:12,555
the princess said, smiling.

136
00:09:13,209 --> 00:09:19,145
At the same moment, the whole castle
woke up, as if nobody had slept for even

137
00:09:19,195 --> 00:09:20,395
a minute.

138
00:09:26,927 --> 00:09:31,147
The king and queen opened their
eyes, the cook stirred her pot,

139
00:09:31,275 --> 00:09:36,022
the horses shook their manes, and
the pigeons flew up into the sky.

140
00:09:37,118 --> 00:09:41,290
The news spread across the whole
kingdom, and everyone came to see the

141
00:09:41,340 --> 00:09:44,754
princess who had woken
up after a hundred years.

142
00:09:45,384 --> 00:09:49,256
That night, the forgotten fairy
appeared at the garden gate,

143
00:09:49,370 --> 00:09:53,756
alone and very quiet,
holding a bunch of roses.

144
00:09:54,368 --> 00:09:59,124
I was hurt because I was forgotten, but
I should never have cast that spell,

145
00:09:59,174 --> 00:10:01,332
and I am sorry with all my heart,

146
00:10:01,382 --> 00:10:04,407
the forgotten fairy said, ashamed.

147
00:10:05,048 --> 00:10:08,709
I forgive you, and from now on
we will never forget anyone,

148
00:10:08,759 --> 00:10:11,424
because everybody deserves
a place at the party,

149
00:10:11,474 --> 00:10:14,458
the princess answered with a kind smile.

150
00:10:15,073 --> 00:10:19,801
Right away, the king ordered a
thirteenth golden plate to be made,

151
00:10:19,851 --> 00:10:23,306
so that no fairy would
ever be left out again.

152
00:10:23,950 --> 00:10:28,997
Soon after, the princess and the prince
had a wedding party in the garden,

153
00:10:29,047 --> 00:10:32,238
full of roses, music, and cake.

154
00:10:32,876 --> 00:10:37,673
And this time all thirteen fairies
were invited, and each one ate from her

155
00:10:37,723 --> 00:10:39,804
very own golden plate.

156
00:10:40,450 --> 00:10:44,664
Popcorn landed on the garden
wall, straightened her red bow,

157
00:10:44,714 --> 00:10:47,517
and watched the party, full of joy.

158
00:10:48,132 --> 00:10:49,509
Hoo, hoo!

159
00:10:49,630 --> 00:10:54,723
Nobody should be left out, and forgiveness
can turn even a spell into a happy

160
00:10:54,773 --> 00:10:55,606
ending,

161
00:10:55,656 --> 00:10:59,056
Popcorn said in her soft and sweet voice.

162
00:10:59,702 --> 00:11:04,777
And the princess lived happily ever
after, sleeping a peaceful sleep every

163
00:11:04,827 --> 00:11:08,450
night, for eight hours
and not a minute more.

164
00:11:15,737 --> 00:11:16,937
The End.

165
00:11:18,644 --> 00:11:19,356
Hoo...

166
00:11:19,406 --> 00:11:20,430
Psst!

167
00:11:20,480 --> 00:11:22,052
Are you still awake?

168
00:11:22,205 --> 00:11:24,259
Did you like tonight's story?

169
00:11:24,366 --> 00:11:28,704
The princess and Popcorn showed
us that nobody should be left out,

170
00:11:28,754 --> 00:11:33,099
and that forgiveness can turn
even a spell into a happy ending.

171
00:11:33,370 --> 00:11:37,676
Good night, sleep tight, and
have the sweetest dreams.

172
00:11:37,972 --> 00:11:42,870
Grown-ups: if you enjoyed it,
please subscribe to Popcorn Tales,

173
00:11:42,920 --> 00:11:45,325
for more stories at bedtime.

174
00:11:45,629 --> 00:11:46,829
Hoo...

